Subject: [PATCH] egl/surfaceless: use the primary node without a render node

The chopin display driver exposes only a primary node (card0); the Mali GPU
is driven through renderonly, which GBM already uses from card0. The
surfaceless platform probed render nodes only, so eglInitialize() failed
and WebKitGTK's web process, which renders through surfaceless EGL,
aborted. Fall back to the primary node for devices without a render node.

--- a/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_surfaceless.c
+++ b/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_surfaceless.c
@@ -245,12 +245,19 @@
       return false;
 
    for (i = 0; i < num_devices; ++i) {
+      unsigned type = node_type;
+
       device = devices[i];
 
-      if (!(device->available_nodes & (1 << node_type)))
+      /* Display controllers whose GPU is driven through renderonly (kmsro)
+       * may expose no render node; open their primary node as GBM does. */
+      if (!swrast && !(device->available_nodes & (1 << DRM_NODE_RENDER)))
+         type = DRM_NODE_PRIMARY;
+
+      if (!(device->available_nodes & (1 << type)))
          continue;
 
-      dri2_dpy->fd = loader_open_device(device->nodes[node_type]);
+      dri2_dpy->fd = loader_open_device(device->nodes[type]);
       if (dri2_dpy->fd < 0)
          continue;
 
